  "text": "8.2 1. When the sun is out, we can't see the stars. 2. Another name for Mars is the red planet because of its colour. 3. Whether or not we like it, governments spend lots of money on space exploration. 4. People who first travelled in space ate dried food that they added water to. 5. When there are many bright lights at night, it's hard to see the stars. 6. It takes more than an hour for light from the sun to reach the planet Saturn.",
